# Framework rules: $project_name

Static reading of the code misses some framework semantics: how transactions begin and end, what rolls back on an error, where authorization is enforced, and what runs on other threads. Kiro applies the rules in this file before it states an end state, a rollback, a commit or an authorization fact.

Ask the team to fill this in for $stack. Keep each rule short and say how to check it in code. A Java and Spring example ships with the tool (`framework_rules: "java-spring"`); use it as a model.

